    {
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50130686",
      "title": "Ask HN: How much are developers trusting LLMs to write prod code?",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "I&#x27;ve been out of the dev role for a few years. I&#x27;d appreciate if you could help me better understand what its actually like out there. How much are you trusting LLMs for writing production code:<p>1. Chat-esque LLM assistance while mostly hand writing code<p>2. LLM writes the code and you review line by line<p>3. Review mainly the high level design and tests, scanning the lower level implementation for stuff that jumps out<p>4. Relying on LLM generated reviews and inspecting what it highlights<p>5. Relying on agentic code&#x2F;PR&#x2F;fix loops<p>How long ago did you hit that level of trust, was it tied to a model release?<p>Are expectations, team norms etc forcing you to use LLMs beyond your trust in it?<p>Have the industry changes brought more excitement about or apathy towards your work?",
