    {
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50135854",
      "title": "How do you deal with AI Output of your boss?",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "So, my boss goes on a rampage. You can clearly see the joy and at the same time the rage and impatience. AI is the tool he always wanted. We are too slow. Process is out of the window. No need for sprints anymore. No planning, just doing. All people downstream must somehow adapt.<p>Whenever i see now his automated messages in slack, my natural reaction is: why do i even bother reading that? Thats for machines to read. He does not need me? Clearly i am not made for that. What is he expecting me to do? To confirm how great the AI did the job? Should i remember all these perfect presentations AI has created and integrate it into my doings into the coming weeks?<p>I am torn. Should i really free my AI and deal with all this incoming text? Is this the way to react on this perfection?<p>I am not mad at him, it clearly frees him of all the burder of dealing with people.<p>I just dont know how to deal with this output personally. It is not for humans.<p>I feel left alone. This is not a company anymore. Everyone is talking to AI now. This feels like chaos. Where everyone can do everything and stepping into each other&#x27;s domain and it is perfect. The only way AI is stopped at are the ACLs.<p>And because AI does everything for me, i don&#x27;t remember things anymore, as i have no emotion connected with it. Feels like bad schooling and memoizing and get through it and you can&#x27;t as it so dry and lifeless.<p>So, how people deal with it in a company context? How have they setup their machines to react and still be up to date without reading the constant stream of changes coming from others?",
      "author": "okr",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-17T22:42:47Z",
      "engagement": 5,
      "tags": [
